🎵
"Pitch notes"/en
===
¶Sing or hum, and see the note you're making — twice. The left note reads the raw @Pitch and jitters; the right note averages the last several pitches and holds steady. @Pitch says 0hz when it hears nothing clear, so both notes skip those moments and show · instead.¶
notes: ['A' 'A♯' 'B' 'C' 'C♯' 'D' 'D♯' 'E' 'F' 'F♯' 'G' 'G♯']
noteOf: ƒ(hz•#hz) hz > 0hz ? notes[(((((12 × (hz ÷ 440hz).log(2)).round()) % 12) + 12) % 12) + 1] '·'
smooth: ƒ(signal•…#hz) (
	heard: (←← 8 signal).sansAll(0hz)
	(heard.combined(0hz ƒ(total•#hz v•#hz) total + v) ÷ heard.length()) ?? 0hz
)
pitch: Pitch()
Stage([
	Group(Stack() [
		Phrase('noisy' color: Color(60% 90 30°))
		Phrase(noteOf(pitch) size: 6m color: Color(60% 90 30°))
	] place: Place(-4m 0m))
	Group(Stack() [
		Phrase('smooth' color: Color(70% 90 240°))
		Phrase(noteOf(smooth(pitch)) size: 6m color: Color(70% 90 240°))
	] place: Place(4m 0m))
])
